        ":question/id": "2ab2c24d-7d61-5976-acd1-acab7ad4094a",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-42008",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{21}$ and ${a}_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\u27f6\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form."
      },
