        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\,\u27f6\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form."
